{"schema":"asx.scenario.v2","id":"sync-rwlock-arrival-order-001","description":"t.w0 write-locks rw and holds it to 100. While it holds, t.r1 (read, at 10), t.w2 (write, at 20), t.r3 (read, at 30) and t.r4 (read, at 40) queue. Rust's release_writer admits the readers that arrived before the first queued writer (t.r1) ahead of it; t.r1's release hands t.w2 the lock; t.w2's release admits t.r3 and t.r4 together (sync/rwlock.rs:531, should_wake_writer). C used to serve the oldest writer first whenever one waited (bd-rm2d).","unit":"sync","rules":["inv.determinism.replayable"],"seed":42,"lab":{"max_steps":600},"regions":[{"name":"r.main","parent":"root","budget":null}],"channels":[],"sync":[{"name":"rw","type":"rwlock"}],"tasks":[{"name":"t.w0","region":"r.main","budget":null,"program":[{"op":"rwlock_write","rwlock":"rw"},{"op":"trace","message":"t.w0 holds"},{"op":"sleep","ns":100},{"op":"rwlock_unlock","rwlock":"rw"}]},{"name":"t.r1","region":"r.main","budget":null,"program":[{"op":"sleep","ns":10},{"op":"rwlock_read","rwlock":"rw"},{"op":"trace","message":"t.r1 holds"},{"op":"sleep","ns":50},{"op":"rwlock_unlock","rwlock":"rw"}]},{"name":"t.w2","region":"r.main","budget":null,"program":[{"op":"sleep","ns":20},{"op":"rwlock_write","rwlock":"rw"},{"op":"trace","message":"t.w2 holds"},{"op":"sleep","ns":50},{"op":"rwlock_unlock","rwlock":"rw"}]},{"name":"t.r3","region":"r.main","budget":null,"program":[{"op":"sleep","ns":30},{"op":"rwlock_read","rwlock":"rw"},{"op":"trace","message":"t.r3 holds"},{"op":"sleep","ns":50},{"op":"rwlock_unlock","rwlock":"rw"}]},{"name":"t.r4","region":"r.main","budget":null,"program":[{"op":"sleep","ns":40},{"op":"rwlock_read","rwlock":"rw"},{"op":"trace","message":"t.r4 holds"},{"op":"yield"},{"op":"rwlock_unlock","rwlock":"rw"}]}],"script":[],"expect":{"kind":"ok"}}
